

[2026-01-27]
Key: svg_substrate:ring_not_closed_skipped
TITLE: SVG substrate rebuild skipped ring_not_closed features
MISTAKE:
The experimental SVG-derived substrate rebuild treated ring_not_closed as invalid and skipped those geometries, dropping settlements even though deterministic closure (repeat first coordinate at end) is allowed under project constraints.
CORRECT RULE:
Do not skip on ring_not_closed. If a ring has >= 4 points, close it deterministically by appending the first coordinate if missing, then revalidate. Only skip if still invalid after closure or if too_few_points/non_finite.

[2026-01-27]
Key: svg_substrate:duplicate_sid_not_merged
TITLE: SVG substrate rebuild emitted duplicate SIDs as separate features
MISTAKE:
The experimental SVG-derived substrate rebuild emitted multiple features with the same SID, violating 1:1 settlement identity in the output GeoJSON (duplicate SIDs existed in source shapes and were not merged).
CORRECT RULE:
Group features by SID and merge duplicates deterministically into a single MultiPolygon feature. Preserve per-part provenance in properties.parts and keep only canonical identity fields at top-level.
CORRECT BEHAVIOR GOING FORWARD:
Fixed 2026-01-27: Canonical substrate derivation script (derive_settlement_substrate_from_svg_sources.ts) now merges duplicate SIDs deterministically into MultiPolygon features with properties.parts preserving per-part provenance. This is enforced in the canonical derive pipeline. Duplicate SIDs are detected, grouped, and merged before output.

[2026-01-27]
Key: viewer:file_protocol_cors_blocking
TITLE: Substrate viewers fail with unclear error when opened via file:// protocol
MISTAKE:
Substrate viewers (both Phase 0 canonical and experimental SVG) use fetch() to load data_index.json and GeoJSON files. When opened directly via file:// protocol, browsers block these requests with CORS errors, but the error messages are unclear ("Failed to fetch" or generic alerts) and don't explain that a local web server is required.
CORRECT RULE:
Detect file:// protocol in viewer loadData() functions. If window.location.protocol === 'file:', show a clear error message explaining that browsers block local file access and provide instructions to run a local web server (e.g., "npx http-server -p 8080" from repo root, then open http://localhost:8080/data/derived/[viewer]/index.html). Update both build scripts to generate viewers with this detection.
CORRECT BEHAVIOR GOING FORWARD:
Fixed 2026-01-27: Canonical substrate viewer (build_substrate_viewer_index.ts) now generates viewer.js with file:// protocol detection. When file:// is detected, an in-page error box is displayed (not alert) with clear instructions: run "npx http-server -p 8080" from repo root, then open "http://localhost:8080/data/derived/substrate_viewer/index.html". This is enforced in generated viewer.js and HTML templates.

